20,12456,3815]},{"label":"Dividends paid","value":"$1.0B","sub":"vs $800M","delta":"+16.8%","tone":"up","spark":[245,244,244,244,242]},{"label":"Stock-based compensation","value":"$6.4B","sub":"vs $4.7B","delta":"+34.8%","tone":"flat","foot":"3.0% of revenue","spark":[1321,1474,1625,1654,1633]},{"label":"Diluted shares (weighted avg.)","value":"24,514M","sub":"vs 24,804M","delta":"−1.2%","tone":"up","spark":[24705,24611,24532,24483,24430],"sparkK":"sh"}]}],"footnotes":["Fiscal 2026 is the year ended Jan 25, 2026; fiscal 2025 ended Jan 26, 2025.","Gross margin includes a $4.5B Q1 charge for excess H20 inventory and purchase obligations. Segment operating income excludes $8.9B of unallocated items, mainly stock-based compensation.","Diluted EPS by quarter as reported in the 10-Qs; fourth quarters are calculated (net income ÷ estimated diluted shares) because EPS does not add across quarters.","Geography is by customer headquarters. Net cash = cash & marketable securities − debt. Free cash flow as reported by NVIDIA."],"report":{"summary":["NVIDIA's revenue rose 65% to $215.9B in fiscal 2026, the year ended January 25, 2026. Data Center grew 68% to $193.7B and made up about 90% of sales. Operating income rose 60% to $130.4B and net income 65% to $120.1B, or $4.90 per diluted share.","Gross margin fell to 71.1% from 75.0%, partly because of a $4.5B first-quarter charge for excess H20 inventory and purchase obligations. Free cash flow was $96.6B, and NVIDIA returned $41.1B to shareholders through buybacks and dividends."],"highlights":["Data Center networking revenue more than doubled, up 142% to $31.4B.","Q4 revenue reached a record $68.1B, up 73% from a year earlier.","Gaming grew 41% to $16.0B and Professional Visualization 70% to $3.2B.","Cash and marketable securities rose to $62.6B against $8.5B of debt."],"watch":["Revenue is concentrated: Data Center was about 90% of the total.","China revenue (including Hong Kong) fell 21% to $19.7B, and Q1 FY2027 guidance of ab